-- title:
--   Maximal ideal at a crossing: branch ideal plus one generator
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and a term $\mathfrak X$ of `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a bundle of data and properties for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the modular curve over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ (properness, flatness and integrality of `DRModel.toBase p`, integral closedness of its sections on affine opens, rational and geometric curve models with their compatibilities, the two sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$, a smooth locus, and the further components of that structure). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two component maps $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$, and let $x =$ `𝔛.crossingPt O κ toκ n` be its image in the base change `baseChangeO p O` $=$ `DRModel p` $\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z} \operatorname{Spec} O$ under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ followed by the base-change map along $\mathrm{to}\kappa$ (composed with the first projection). Assume the two generic points $\xi_\infty = \mathfrak X.\xi\mathrm{inf}$ and $\xi_0 = \mathfrak X.\xi\mathrm{zero}$ each specialise to $x$, witnessed by `hinf` and `hzero`. Then, writing $R$ for the stalk of `baseChangeO p O` at $x$ and $\mathfrak m_R$ for its maximal ideal, there exist $t_1, t_2 \in R$ with $\mathfrak m_R = P + (t_1)$ and $\mathfrak m_R = Q + (t_2)$, where $P$ (resp. $Q$) is `Scheme.branchIdeal hinf` (resp. `Scheme.branchIdeal hzero`), the preimage of the maximal ideal of the stalk at $\xi_\infty$ (resp. at $\xi_0$) under the specialisation map $R \to \mathcal O_{\xi_\infty}$ (resp. $R \to \mathcal O_{\xi_0}$).
--
--   The statement expresses, in a form avoiding quotient rings, that each of the two branches of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model over $O$ is regular at a crossing point: modulo the branch ideal the maximal ideal of the local ring becomes principal. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal) in the local analysis of the crossing points of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_exists_maximalIdeal_eq_branchIdeal_sup_span_singleton.lean

